    "No query-specific hepatic clearance or metabolic stability experiment; L6 records are for reference molecules.",
    "C19 is a close but not identical analogue and its low-F outcome is qualitative.",
    "Napsagatran hepatic clearance data are rat-only; human transfer is uncertain."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted low and kept: the query is a fully ionized zwitterionic benzamidine and carboxylate peptidomimetic with logD -7.48 and TPSA 148.6. The most transferable direct low-F context (C19) reports absolute oral bioavailability not high enough for oral use in humans for a similarly benzamidine and carboxylate rich molecule. L5 human jejunal permeability and efflux evidence supports poor absorption. L6 hepatic evidence is mixed: napsagatran shows moderate rat hepatic intrinsic clearance (C78, C84) while dabigatran shows no CYP metabolism and low glucuronidation clearance (C76, C73, C74, C79-C82); this does not overturn the permeability-driven low prediction. Confidence stays moderate because all mechanistic records are for reference molecules, not the query."
}

